# Personal Finance Manager — Cursor Rules
# These rules give Claude Code the same context as the Cowork session.

## Project Overview
You are working on a Personal Finance Manager (PFM) — a full-stack app for tracking
bank transactions, stock portfolios (Simply Wall St), and investment properties.
It runs locally on Mac for a single user (Hardik Sanghavi).

## Memory System
This project uses a two-tier memory system. Always check these before starting work:
1. **CLAUDE.md** (this directory) — hot cache with terms, decisions, build plan
2. **memory/** directory — deep context (glossary, project details, existing schema)

Read CLAUDE.md first for every task. If you encounter unfamiliar terms or acronyms,
check memory/glossary.md before asking.

## Tech Stack
- **Backend:** Python FastAPI + async SQLAlchemy 2.0 + aiomysql
- **Frontend:** React (Vite + Recharts + Tailwind CSS), light theme
- **Database:** MariaDB on port 3306, database name `finance_app`
- **Docker:** docker-compose in this directory (MariaDB + phpMyAdmin)
- **Tests:** pytest + pytest-asyncio (backend), Vite build check (frontend)

## Code Standards
- All Python files must have a module-level docstring explaining purpose
- All JS/JSX files must have a JSDoc comment block at the top
- FastAPI routes use async/await with SQLAlchemy async sessions
- React components are functional with hooks (no class components)
- Tailwind CSS for all styling (no custom CSS files)
- Every chunk of work must include tests

## Architecture Rules
- **Backend serves API only** — no templates, no HTML rendering
- **No AI API calls in the app** — Cowork handles AI categorisation externally
- **Pluggable bank parsers** — each bank has its own parser class extending base.py
- **Dedup via SHA256 hash** of (account_id + tx_date + tx_desc + tx_amount)
- **CORS enabled** — backend on port 8000, frontend on port 5173
- **Old code in /src/ is read-only** — never modify it

## Directory Structure
```
finance-app/
├── CLAUDE.md                  # Project memory (read this first!)
├── memory/                    # Deep memory (glossary, project context)
├── docker-compose.yml         # MariaDB 3306 + phpMyAdmin 8080
├── run.sh                     # Start/stop/setup script
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py            # FastAPI app entry point
│   │   ├── config.py          # Settings from .env
│   │   ├── database.py        # Async SQLAlchemy engine
│   │   ├── models.py          # ORM models (Chunk 2)
│   │   ├── schemas.py         # Pydantic schemas (Chunk 2)
│   │   ├── routers/           # API route handlers
│   │   ├── parsers/           # Bank CSV parsers (ABC pattern)
│   │   ├── services/          # Business logic layer
│   │   └── utils/             # Helpers (hashing, CSV utils)
│   ├── tests/                 # pytest test files
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   └── .env                   # DB credentials (local only)
└── frontend/
    ├── src/
    │   ├── App.jsx            # React Router setup
    │   ├── api/               # Axios API client modules
    │   ├── components/        # Reusable UI components
    │   ├── pages/             # Page-level components
    │   └── hooks/             # Custom React hooks
    ├── vite.config.js         # Vite + Tailwind + API proxy
    └── package.json
```

## Build Plan (Phase 1)
Check CLAUDE.md for the current status of each chunk. The build follows
incremental vertical slices — each chunk delivers working backend + frontend + tests.

## Workflow Preferences
- Ask clarifying questions before making changes
- Show progress percentage on multi-step tasks
- Test each piece before moving to the next
- Update CLAUDE.md after completing each chunk
- Never skip writing tests
